# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/ExpandedLicensing/standardAdditionTemplate node144
node144 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>standardAdditionTemplate</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/ExpandedLicensing/standardAdditionTemplate' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/ExpandedLicensing/standardAdditionTemplate</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;Identifies the full text of a LicenseAddition, in SPDX templating format.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;Identifies the full text of a LicenseAddition, in SPDX templating format.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;A standardAdditionTemplate contains a license addition template which describes
sections of the LicenseAddition text which can be varied.

See the Legacy Text Template format section of the
SPDX License List Matching Guidelines
for format information.

It is recommended to use licenseXml instead, as it can
capture all the text and metadata associated with a license.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
