# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/iscc node412
node412 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>iscc</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/iscc' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/iscc</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;International Standard Content Code (ISCC) &lt;https://iscc.io/&gt; is a content-derived identifier standardized by ISO 24138 &lt;https://www.iso.org/standard/77899.html&gt; for identifying digital assets. ISCC can be used in conjunction with other schemes, such as DOI, ISAN, ISBN, ISRC, ISSN and ISWC. A standard ISCC-CODE is build from multiple ISCC-UNITs. Each unit serve a different purpose. An ISCC-CODE typically look like ISCC:KACT4EBWK27737D2AYCJRAL5Z36G76RFRMO4554RU26HZ4ORJGIVHDI.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;International Standard Content Code (ISCC) &lt;https://iscc.io/&gt; is a content-derived identifier standardized by ISO 24138 &lt;https://www.iso.org/standard/77899.html&gt; for identifying digital assets. ISCC can be used in conjunction with other schemes, such as DOI, ISAN, ISBN, ISRC, ISSN and ISWC. A standard ISCC-CODE is build from multiple ISCC-UNITs. Each unit serve a different purpose. An ISCC-CODE typically look like ISCC:KACT4EBWK27737D2AYCJRAL5Z36G76RFRMO4554RU26HZ4ORJGIVHDI.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/EnergyConsumptionDescription node413
node413 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>EnergyConsumptionDescription</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/EnergyConsumptionDescription' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/EnergyConsumptionDescription</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;The class that helps note down the quantity of energy consumption and the unit
used for measurement.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;The class that helps note down the quantity of energy consumption and the unit
used for measurement.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;This class is designed to store energy consumption data, including the quantity
and the unit of measurement.

The energyQuantity property stores the amount of energy consumed,
and the energyUnit property stores the unit used for measurement.

For example, 0.042 kilowatt-hour of energy will have 0.042 as a value for
property energyQuantity, and &quot;kilowattHour&quot; as a value for property
energyUnit.

*Example*

{
  &quot;type&quot;: &quot;ai_EnergyConsumptionDescription&quot;,
  &quot;ai_energyQuantity&quot;: &quot;0.042&quot;,
  &quot;ai_energyUnit&quot;: &quot;kilowattHour&quot;
}&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isil node414
node414 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>isil</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isil' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isil</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;International Standard Identifier for Libraries and Related Organizations (ISIL) &lt;https://slks.dk/english/work-areas/libraries-and-literature/library-standards/isil/&gt; is a unique alphanumeric code for identifying libraries, archives, museums, and related organizations standardized by ISO 15511 &lt;https://www.iso.org/standard/77849.html&gt;. It consists of a prefix—which may be an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code or a non-country code assigned by the ISIL Registration Authority—followed by a unit identifier, totaling up to 16 characters (e.g., FI-Sipoo-Sö or ZDB-1-SBD). Valid symbols include any alphanumeric character, solidus (/), hyphen-minus (-), or colon.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;International Standard Identifier for Libraries and Related Organizations (ISIL) &lt;https://slks.dk/english/work-areas/libraries-and-literature/library-standards/isil/&gt; is a unique alphanumeric code for identifying libraries, archives, museums, and related organizations standardized by ISO 15511 &lt;https://www.iso.org/standard/77849.html&gt;. It consists of a prefix—which may be an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code or a non-country code assigned by the ISIL Registration Authority—followed by a unit identifier, totaling up to 16 characters (e.g., FI-Sipoo-Sö or ZDB-1-SBD). Valid symbols include any alphanumeric character, solidus (/), hyphen-minus (-), or colon.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/SsvcDecisionType/attend node415
node415 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>attend</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/SsvcDecisionType/attend' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/SsvcDecisionType/attend</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;The vulnerability requires attention from the organization&#x27;s internal, supervisory-level individuals. Necessary actions include requesting assistance or information about the vulnerability, and may involve publishing a notification either internally and/or externally. CISA recommends remediating Attend vulnerabilities sooner than standard update timelines.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;The vulnerability requires attention from the organization&#x27;s internal, supervisory-level individuals. Necessary actions include requesting assistance or information about the vulnerability, and may involve publishing a notification either internally and/or externally. CISA recommends remediating Attend vulnerabilities sooner than standard update timelines.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/headquartersLocation node416
node416 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>headquartersLocation</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/headquartersLocation' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/headquartersLocation</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;The headquartersLocation defines the location of the organization&#x27;s headquarters.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;The headquartersLocation defines the location of the organization&#x27;s headquarters.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;Headquarters denotes the location where most or all of the important functions of an organization are coordinated. In the United States, the corporate headquarters represents the entity at the center or the top of a corporation taking full responsibility for managing all business activities.
To identify an organization&#x27;s headquarters accurately, you provide address information (mailing, street and GPL) information related to the organization’s headquarters.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Hardware/BulkHardware node417
node417 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>BulkHardware</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Hardware/BulkHardware' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Hardware/BulkHardware</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;Products or commodities produced as a bulk unit are called bulk products. Commodities are often sold in bulk.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;Products or commodities produced as a bulk unit are called bulk products. Commodities are often sold in bulk.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;Products or commodities produced as a bulk unit are called bulk products. Commodities are often sold in bulk based on a batch or bulk ID number associated with the bulk unit.
Bulk units defined in the QUDT Units standards.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
