node1101 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>bic</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/bic' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/bic</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;Business Identifier Code (BIC), also known as SWIFT-BIC or SWIFT code, is a unique 8 or 11-character alphanumeric code standardized by ISO 9362 &lt;https://www.iso.org/standard/84108.html&gt; to identify financial and non-financial institutions (e.g., BBWCUS33).&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;Business Identifier Code (BIC), also known as SWIFT-BIC or SWIFT code, is a unique 8 or 11-character alphanumeric code standardized by ISO 9362 &lt;https://www.iso.org/standard/84108.html&gt; to identify financial and non-financial institutions (e.g., BBWCUS33).&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
